{"kind":"request","text":"Replace the source-text pins in the shared-selection focus test with behavioural ones. In ui/test/interaction.test.mjs at commit 00b7070d872ad404ebc47679504881ebab6d16eb, the test 'task and event surfaces wire shared selection to advisory focus' reads WorkDrawer.tsx and TopBar.tsx with readFileSync and asserts four regexes against their source text: the onSelect/onOpenThread pair, actor.focus.includes(event), toggleActivityFocus(session.activity.focus, selectedEvent), and setActivity({ focus: [] }). A source regex fails in both directions at once. It misses the break, because deleting a render site leaves the matched text in place; and it catches the harmless refactor, because rewriting includes(event) to indexOf(event) \u003e= 0 turns the test red with the behaviour unchanged. The review that approved this head measured exactly that: the equivalent Stream regex was removed and its indexOf rewrite is now green, while this one still reddens. WorkDrawer's rendering is separately and correctly pinned through rendered SSR markup, so this regex sits redundantly on top of a working behavioural pin.","body":{"conditions":"Each of the four assertions is either replaced by one that exercises the behaviour through rendered markup or an invoked handler, or deleted as redundant where a behavioural pin already holds the same property, with the redundancy demonstrated by breaking the production site and watching the surviving test fail. Rewriting actor.focus.includes(event) to actor.focus.indexOf(event) \u003e= 0 leaves the UI suite green, and deleting any one of the focus render sites leaves it red, both demonstrated by applying the change alone and reverting it. Full UI suite, tsc, npm build, make ui-check byte-identical, go vet and go test green. Approved at an exact head by a reviewer other than the author.","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}